@@ -446,6 +446,17 @@ The library also supports convenient formatting of ranges and tuples::
   // Prints "('a', 1, 2.0)"
   fmt::print("{}", t);
 
+By default, non-string character ranges are formatted as lists of quoted
+characters, including nested ranges and C++20 range views::
+
+  #include <fmt/ranges.h>
+  #include <ranges>
+  #include <string>
+
+  std::string line = "a,b-c,d-e,f";
+  // Prints "[['a'], ['b', '-', 'c'], ['d', '-', 'e'], ['f']]"
+  fmt::print("{}", line | std::views::split(','));
+
 
 NOTE: currently, the overload of ``fmt::join`` for iterables exists in the main
 ``format.h`` header, but expect this to change in the future.
